  "facts": [
    "Borden Avenue Bridge, designed by Edward Abraham Byrne, opened March 25, 1908, and remains one of only four retractable bridges left in the United States.",
    "Its main span stretches 84 feet, sliding on rails to allow marine traffic, a feature last employed in 2005 to clear Dutch Kills.",
    "The bridge is one of just two remaining retractable structures in New York City, the other being the historic Carroll Street Bridge."
